ector"},{"text":"Airport General Manager"},{"text":"Airport Operations Director"}]},{"type":"h","text":"What Employers Usually Test"},{"type":"p","text":"Employers commonly assess:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airport knowledge"},{"text":"Ground handling"},{"text":"Passenger handling"},{"text":"Aircraft turnaround"},{"text":"Aviation safety"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Customer service"},{"text":"Problem solving"},{"text":"Emergency response"},{"text":"Team coordination"},{"text":"Shift readiness"},{"text":"Operational reporting"},{"text":"Basic aviation regulations"},{"text":"Stress management"},{"text":"Situational judgement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Scenario"},{"type":"p","text":"An arriving flight is delayed, its gate is occupied, connecting passengers are waiting, and the next scheduled departure is approaching."},{"type":"p","text":"An Airport Operations Executive should:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Verify the operational status."},{"text":"Coordinate with the airline/operations control."},{"text":"Check alternative gate/stand availability."},{"text":"Coordinate passenger movement."},{"text":"Communicate with relevant ground teams."},{"text":"Reassess the aircraft turnaround timeline."},{"text":"Coordinate baggage and other turnaround services."},{"text":"Identify connecting-passenger priorities."},{"text":"Escalate operational risks appropriately."},{"text":"Keep stakeholders updated."},{"text":"Document the disruption."},{"text":"Monitor the revised operation until normal flow is restored."}]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is to maintain safety while minimising operational disruption and passenger impact."},{"type":"h","text":"Government / Public-Sector Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential aviation environments include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government airport organisations"},{"text":"Airport authorities"},{"text":"Civil aviation departments"},{"text":"Public-sector aviation organisations"},{"text":"Government-su